{#- The voice-drift decision item's context (`voice_drift.build_item`), which
    `decide/user.j2` shows above the question.
    Vars: name (str), anchor (str, never empty -- the judge only runs for
    characters that have one), transcript (str, rendered via
    snippets/transcript.j2), correction (str, optional).

    `correction` is the character's OUTSTANDING drift note, and the caller is
    responsible for having checked that it is still in force -- see
    `voice_drift.judge_item`, which `_stage_voice_drift` builds through. The scene prompt tells the writer a correction
    outranks the anchor, so a judge that could not see it would flag the model
    for obeying the instruction it was given, and the flag would mint another
    correction. Omitted entirely when there is none, so a character without one
    produces the text this template always produced. -#}
Character: {{ name }}

Voice anchor:
{{ anchor }}
{% if correction %}
Outstanding correction (more recent than the anchor; supersedes it on conflict):
{{ correction }}
{% endif %}
Scene transcript:
{{ transcript }}
